
BM25 finds text that contains the important words from the query, and scores how well each document/chunk matches those words.

Ex:

                   BM25
                    │
             query: "fox deer"
                    │
          ┌─────────┴─────────┐
          ↓                   ↓
     query terms          all chunks
                              │
                    ┌─────────┼─────────┐
                    ↓         ↓         ↓
                  Chunk 1   Chunk 2   Chunk 3
                    │         │         │
                 score      score      score
                    │         │         │
                    └─────────┼─────────┘
                              ↓
                         ranked results

our vector search - Which chunk has the most similar meaning?
BM25 asks something different - Which chunk contains the important words from my query?


BM25 score
   │
   ├── TF
   │     └── does the term occur, and how often?
   │           ↳ diminishing returns
   │
   ├── IDF
   │     └── how rare is the term across chunks?
   │
   └── document-length normalization
         └── don't unfairly favor long chunks

first few occurrences of a vocab -
        → useful increase

many more occurrences of a vocab -
        → progressively smaller increase
          i.e instead of using TF as a score (aka weight), a normalized scope is determined.
              this calculation based on IDF, TF, length of doc in words, average lenght of doc, 2 hyper parameters

                 BM25 score (aka weight)
                     │
        ┌────────────┼────────────┐
        ↓            ↓            ↓
       IDF          TF       length normalization
        │            │            │
   rarity across   frequency   this doc vs
   all documents   in this doc  average doc
                     │
                     ↓
              2 hyperparameters


                 Query
                   │
          ┌────────┴────────┐
          ▼                 ▼
      Vector              BM25
          │                 │
       top-k              top-k
          │                 │
          └────────┬────────┘
                   ▼
              combine/rank
                   │
                   ▼
             final chunks
                   │
                   ▼
                  LLM
